```plaintext
0result.sql
```

Reason:  
• 0result.sql scans the entire season, pairing every driver‑standing row with the constructor he drove for in that particular race and then takes MAX(points); this guarantees the best season‑total that was actually earned while the driver was with that constructor.  
• 1result.sql and 2result.sql look only at the final race of each year. A driver who changed teams mid‑season will be counted only for the constructor he drove for in that last race, so any points he scored earlier for his previous team are lost; thus their numbers can be understated (or overstated) for constructors that experienced driver changes.  
• All three queries return the same top‑3 for the current data snapshot, but 0result.sql is logically correct for every season, even when intra‑season driver moves occur.